  { question: 'Can you build strength with only dumbbells?', answer: 'Yes. Dumbbells can provide enough resistance for many people to build strength and muscle when exercises are progressed over time. The key is using movements that cover the major patterns and gradually increasing difficulty, load, repetitions or control.' },
  { question: 'How many days per week should I do a dumbbell workout?', answer: 'Two or three full-body sessions per week can work well for many beginners and intermediate exercisers. The right schedule depends on experience, recovery, goals and other activity.' },
  { question: 'What if my dumbbells are too light?', answer: 'You can make a light dumbbell harder by using more repetitions, slower lowering, pauses, single-leg or single-arm variations and larger ranges of motion. Eventually, heavier resistance may still be useful.' },
  { question: 'Do I need an adjustable bench?', answer: 'No. A bench is helpful but not required. Floor presses, split squats, rows supported on a chair and standing presses can cover most of the same basic movement patterns.' }
];

